# SPEC — `cc-workflow` source adapter

## 1. Identity & root

| field | value |
|---|---|
| `id` | `cc-workflow` |
| env var | `PI_CC_WORKFLOW_DIR` (matches `PI_SESSIONS_DIR` / `CLAUDE_SESSIONS_DIR` pattern in `pi.js:30`, `claude-code.js:65`) |
| `DEFAULT_ROOT` | `path.join(os.homedir(), '.pi', 'cc-workflow', 'runs')` |
| `defaultRoot()` | `process.env.PI_CC_WORKFLOW_DIR || DEFAULT_ROOT` |

New file: `src/sources/cc-workflow.js`.

## 2. `discover(root)`

Flat scan only (runs dir has no subdirs — confirmed via `ls`). Mirror `pi.js:35-50` but **no stack/recursion**:

```js
for (const e of fs.readdirSync(root, {withFileTypes:true})) {
  if (e.isFile() && e.name.endsWith('.json')) {
    out.push({
      filePath: path.join(root, e.name),
      source: ID,
      projectKey: e.name.replace(/\.json$/, ''),  // runId-ish; used only for library projectDir fallback
    });
  }
