```

Guard `if (!root || !fs.existsSync(root)) return out;` as in pi.

## 3. `sniff(filePath, firstLine)`

**Problem:** journal files are pretty-printed JSON. `readFirstJsonLine` in `src/sources/index.js:34-48` calls `JSON.parse('{')` → throws → returns `null` → `sniffSource` returns `null` (line 60-66). So `firstLine` will always be `null` for these files.

**Minimal change to `src/sources/index.js`:**
- In `sniffSource(filePath, firstLine)` (line 58), after the `for (const a of ...) { if (a.sniff(filePath, fl)) ... }` loop, **add a second pass** that calls each adapter's `sniff(filePath, null)` so adapters with a "look at the whole file" strategy get a shot. Or simpler: change the existing loop to always call `a.sniff(filePath, fl)` (already does — `fl` will be `null` for cc-workflow), and require this adapter's `sniff` to handle `firstLine === null` itself by reading the file.

Recommended: keep the existing call signature; the adapter's `sniff` checks `firstLine` first (cheap path for the other sources), and on null falls back to bounded file read:

```js
function sniff(filePath, firstLine) {
  // pretty-printed JSON => firstLine is unreadable as JSON; fall back.
  if (firstLine && typeof firstLine === 'object') {
    // If a sibling adapter would have claimed it, we wouldn't get here. But
    // be defensive: only claim a parsed firstLine if it looks like our root.
    return typeof firstLine.runId === 'string' && Array.isArray(firstLine.journal);
  }
  if (!filePath || !filePath.endsWith('.json')) return false;
  try {
    const fd = fs.openSync(filePath, 'r');
    const buf = Buffer.alloc(64 * 1024);
    const n = fs.readSync(fd, buf, 0, buf.length, 0);
    fs.closeSync(fd);
    const head = buf.slice(0, n).toString('utf8');
    // Cheap textual check — avoids parsing 64KB that might be a partial object.
    return /"runId"\s*:/.test(head) && /"journal"\s*:/.test(head);
  } catch { return false; }
}
```

Note: pi and cc both reject `firstLine == null` early, so this adapter is the only one that needs the fallback. **No change needed to `readFirstJsonLine`**, only the single-pass behavior already iterates registry in order — make sure cc-workflow is registered AFTER pi/cc so the cheap paths run first.

## 4. `parseFile(filePath)` — synthesize pi-shape envelope

Read file (apply `MAX_FILE_BYTES` guard like pi.js:69-89), `JSON.parse` whole thing, then synthesize.

```js
const doc = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(filePath,'utf8'));
const journal = Array.isArray(doc.journal) ? doc.journal : [];
const startedAt = typeof doc.startedAt === 'number' ? doc.startedAt : null;
const finishedAt = typeof doc.finishedAt === 'number' ? doc.finishedAt : startedAt;

// linear timestamp interpolation across [startedAt, finishedAt]
const span = (finishedAt != null && startedAt != null) ? finishedAt - startedAt : 0;
const n = journal.length;
const tsFor = (i) => {
  if (startedAt == null) return null;
  if (n <= 1) return new Date(startedAt).toISOString();
  return new Date(startedAt + Math.round(span * (i / Math.max(1, n - 1)))).toISOString();
};

const entries = journal.map((j, i) => {
  const r = j.result;
  const text = (typeof r === 'string') ? r
             : (r == null) ? ''
             : JSON.stringify(r, null, 2);
  return {
    id: `agent-${j.index ?? i}`,
    parentId: null,
    timestamp: tsFor(i),
    raw: j,
    source: ID,
    sidechain: false,
    kind: 'assistant',
    text,
    thinking: '',
    toolCalls: [],
    model: null,
    provider: null,
    api: null,
    usage: null,
    cost: null,
    totalTokens: null,
    stopReason: null,
    responseId: null,
    messageId: null,
    shardOf: null,
  };
});

const sessionMeta = {
  id: doc.runId || path.basename(filePath, '.json'),
  cwd: '',                                  // unknown; summary.js will fall back to decodeProjectDir
  version: '',
  gitBranch: '',
  model: null,
  permissionMode: null,
  tools: [], mcpServers: [], agents: [],
  timestamp: startedAt ? new Date(startedAt).toISOString() : null,
  projectPath: doc.scriptPath || '',        // <-- non-standard field; summary.js does NOT read this (see Risks)
  name: doc.name || '',
  status: doc.status || '',
  synthesized: true,
  source: ID,
};

return { entries, parseErrors: [], sessionMeta, filePath, source: ID };
```

**Recommendation: assistant-only entries** (no synthetic `user` placeholder). Rationale: per `summary.js:21`, `firstPrompt` is taken from `entries.find(e => e.kind==='user')?.text`. With no user entries, `firstPrompt` will be `null`. To satisfy spec item 5 (use name + status), instead set `sessionMeta.cwd = doc.scriptPath` so something useful renders, and **override `firstPrompt`** by — see Risks §10 — patching `summary.js` or piggybacking on a synthetic user. Cleanest: emit ONE leading `kind:'user'` synthetic entry with `text = "${doc.name} (${doc.status})"` and `promptType:'user'`. This makes `userMessageCount=1`, `assistantMessageCount = journal.length`, and `firstPrompt` works without touching `summary.js`. **Revised recommendation: ONE synthetic user + N assistants**, not assistant-only. The cost (one fake row) is far less than special-casing summary.js.

## 5. Summary aggregation

Falls out naturally from §4 if we use the 1-user + N-assistant shape:
- `assistantMessageCount = journal.length` ✓ (via summary.js switch case at `summary.js:71`)
- `userMessageCount = 1`, everything else 0 ✓
- `firstPrompt = "${name} (${status})"` ✓ via existing logic
- `totalTokens = 0`, `totalCost = 0` ✓ (assistant entries have `null`)
- `projectPath`: `summary.js:139-148` `resolveProjectPath` chain — `sessionMeta.cwd` empty, no `raw.cwd` on entries → falls through to `adapter.decodeProjectDir(projectDir)`. Implement `decodeProjectDir(runIdOrName) { return ''; }` (or return the runId itself); but **better**: set `sessionMeta.cwd = doc.scriptPath` so library shows the script path as the project — matches spec item 4 ("library shows the script"). Drop the non-standard `projectMeta.projectPath` field.

Final `sessionMeta.cwd = doc.scriptPath || ''`.

## 6. Registry — `src/sources/index.js`

```js
const ccWorkflow = require('./cc-workflow');
const REGISTRY = { [pi.id]: pi, [claudeCode.id]: claudeCode, [ccWorkflow.id]: ccWorkflow };
```
Order matters (see §3): pi & cc sniffs are O(1) on `firstLine`; cc-workflow's fallback opens the file. Putting it last in REGISTRY = correct.

