## 10. Risks / blast radius

| where | line | concern | mitigation |
|---|---|---|---|
| `src/sources/index.js` | 33-48, 58-66 | `readFirstJsonLine` returns `null` for pretty-printed JSON → sniffSource returns null before our adapter sees it. | Adapter's `sniff` handles `firstLine == null` itself by re-reading the file (bounded 64KB) — no change to `readFirstJsonLine` needed. |
| `src/summary.js` | 21 | `firstPrompt` from first `user` entry. With assistant-only entries it'd be `null`. | Recommendation §4: emit 1 synthetic user. No core change. |
| `src/summary.js` | 139-148 `resolveProjectPath` | Falls through chains; if `sessionMeta.cwd` set to scriptPath, fine. If empty → calls `adapter.decodeProjectDir(projectKey='run-mq…-1')`. | Implement `decodeProjectDir` to return `''` (or scriptPath stem) defensively. Spec sets `cwd=scriptPath` so this path is rarely hit. |
| `src/initial-input.js` | 63, 70 | `source === 'claude-code'` branch; pi-or-else falls through to `loadPi` → `buildInitialInputViaPi` which calls pi's `loadProjectContextFiles` against `cwd`. With `cwd=scriptPath` (a file, not dir) pi may explode. | Add early `if (source === 'cc-workflow') return null;` at line 65 (returns 404 from `/api/sessions/:id/initial-input` — acceptable; workflows don't have an "initial input" concept). |
| `public/app.js` | 627 | Hard ternary `data.source === 'claude-code' ? cc-msg : pi-msg`. cc-workflow sessions get the **pi** message ("reconstructed by buildSystemPrompt()") which is wrong but harmless. | Either guard initial-input UI on the cc-workflow source (recommend: hide the rendered-prompt block when source==='cc-workflow' OR when `data == null`). Low priority — `/initial-input` returning null already triggers the empty state. |
| `src/signals.js` | — | Iterates entries by kind; assistant-only entries with no tool calls / no errors produce 0 signals. ✓ No issue. | none |
| `src/api.js` `globalStats` | 322 | `sourceCounts[s.source]++` — generic, supports any source ✓. | none |
| `test/api.test.js` | 35 | `setSessionsRoot(FIX)` mounts as pi only; if we add cc-workflow files to `fixtures/` later they'd be invisible. | none for this PR. |
| Concurrency / perf | — | `parseFile` reads whole JSON; the 28KB fixture is fine, but a multi-MB journal will JSON.parse all at once. | Add same 256MB cap as siblings; document as known limitation since these files aren't expected to grow large. |
| `setSessionsRoot` back-compat shim | api.js:41 | Currently only zeroes `pi` + `claude-code`. After §8, must also zero `cc-workflow` so tests don't see stray rows. | included in §8. |

No changes needed to `signals.js`, `export-html.js`, `pricing.js`, or `parser.js` (dispatch is generic).

Done. Spec is opinionated: 1 synthetic user + N assistants, `cwd=scriptPath`, sniff fallback in-adapter, registry-order matters.
